Q: SHGetFileInfo on EXE files occasionally incorrectly gives generic app icon system image list index (2), with various flags attempted A: <p><strong>EXEs are annoying because SHGetFileInfo doesn't always give you the right icon through the system image list.</strong></p>
<p><strong>Here's the clean fix:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>Create your own image list.</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Use SHGetFileInfo with SHGFI_ICON to get the HICON directly.</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Add it to your image list using ImageList_AddIcon.</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Use that index in your ListView.</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Let me know if you need more help.&quot;</strong></p>
<p>here is the code that might help u:</p>
<pre><code>// Create a custom image list (if you don't have one)
HIMAGELIST hMyImageList = ImageList_Create(16, 16, ILC_COLOR32 | ILC_MASK, 10, 10);

// For each EXE:
SHFILEINFO sfi;
HICON hIcon = NULL;

// Get the icon directly
if (SHGetFileInfo(fullpath.c_str(), 0, &amp;sfi, sizeof(sfi),
    SHGFI_ICON | SHGFI_SMALLICON | SHGFI_USEFILEATTRIBUTES))
{
    hIcon = sfi.hIcon;
}
else
{
    // Fallback: ExtractIconEx
    ExtractIconEx(fullpath.c_str(), 0, NULL, &amp;hIcon, 1);
}

if (hIcon)
{
    // Add to your custom image list
    int index = ImageList_AddIcon(hMyImageList, hIcon);
    DestroyIcon(hIcon); // Clean up

    // Store index in ListView item
    LVITEM lvi = {0};
    lvi.mask = LVIF_IMAGE;
    lvi.iItem = row;
    lvi.iImage = index;
    ListView_SetItem(hWndListView, &amp;lvi);
}

// Set the custom image list to the ListView
SendMessage(hWndListView, LVM_SETIMAGELIST, LVSIL_SMALL, (LPARAM)hMyImageList);
</code></pre>
